# Normalise line endings in the repository; check out native on Windows.
* text=auto

# The pre-push hook is a shell script, and a shell script with CRLF line
# endings fails on Linux and macOS with "bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M" -- the
# carriage return becomes part of the interpreter path. Git Bash's sh tolerates
# it, which is exactly why testing the hook on Windows cannot catch this.
# Everything here is win-x64 and WPF, so it is unlikely to be cloned elsewhere;
# an unnoticed silently-broken guard is still not worth the saving.
.githooks/pre-push text eol=lf

# Binary assets: never touched.
*.bmp binary
*.ico binary
*.png binary
